From a13c680509f7816fce244601b462df323f5ae0ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dastbe <dastbe@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:25:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] starlark: add 'name = load("module")' to bind a whole module

Behind the new syntax.FileOptions.LoadModule option, a load statement
may appear as the right-hand side of an assignment to a single
identifier, with no symbols listed. The identifier is bound to a
*starlark.LoadedModule whose attributes are the module's exported
(non-underscore) members, so callers can write lib.f().

- syntax: LoadStmt.Alias; parser accepts IDENT '=' load(STRING)
- resolve: Alias is bound like any other load binding
- compile: new LOADMODULE opcode; bytecode Version 15
- starlark: LoadedModule value; LOAD/LOADMODULE share Thread.load

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RQkJsyThCiRZxeZr2ymEyZ
