diff --git a/doc/spec.md b/doc/spec.md
index 29a38cb..4f3d1dc 100644
--- a/doc/spec.md
+++ b/doc/spec.md
@@ -2870,6 +2870,31 @@ load("module.star", "x", y2="y", "z")    # assigns x, y2, and z
 
 A load statement may not be nested inside any other statement.
 
+<b>Implementation note:</b>
+The Go implementation of Starlark permits an additional form of the
+load statement when the `LoadModule` file option is enabled.
+In this form, the load appears on the right-hand side of an assignment
+to a single identifier, and names no symbols to extract:
+
+```grammar {.good}
+LoadModuleStmt = identifier '=' 'load' '(' string [','] ')' .
+```
+
+It binds the identifier to a value of type `module` representing the
+entire loaded module. Its attributes are the module's exported
+globals, that is, those whose names do not start with `_`:
+
+```python
+lib = load("lib.star")
+lib.f(1)                  # calls f, defined in lib.star
+lib._g                    # error: module has no ._g field or method
+```
+
+Like the names bound by an ordinary load statement, the identifier is
+local to the file, and the statement may not be nested inside any
+other statement. `load` is not otherwise an expression:
+`f(load("lib.star"))` is a syntax error.
+
 
 ## Module execution
 
